---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../../lib/siteUrl';
---

<Layout
  title="Colorize Workflow Guide"
  description="Use Varve's tint, selective recolor, palette, reference transfer, harmonize, and model-gated photo colorization workflows."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <main class="docs-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/docs')}>Docs</a> / <a href={sitePath('/docs/tools/color')}>Color &amp; Effects</a> / Colorize
      </nav>
      <h1>Colorize with an explicit source and scope.</h1>
      <p class="docs-intro">
        Select an image and open Adjustments → Colorize. Choose the operation that matches your
        intent; the controls and required inputs change with the mode.
      </p>

      <section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="choose-title">
        <h2 id="choose-title">Choose the workflow</h2>
        <div class="mode-table">
          <article><h3>Tint / Selective Recolor</h3><p>Set an absolute hue or rotate existing hue. Whole image is an explicit scope; mask image limits coverage.</p><span>Offline · no model</span></article>
          <article><h3>Palette Colorize</h3><p>Select document swatches, then choose shaded influence or strict palette bytes.</p><span>Offline · no model</span></article>
          <article><h3>Reference Transfer</h3><p>Choose a separate reference image to transfer its global color distribution. This is not object matching.</p><span>Offline · reference required</span></article>
          <article><h3>Harmonize</h3><p>Move target chroma toward a reference distribution while retaining target structure and source lightness.</p><span>Offline · reference required</span></article>
          <article><h3>Photo Colorization</h3><p>Use local DDColor only when a verified model is installed. It proposes plausible colors, not historical truth.</p><span>Model-gated · artifact status is visible</span></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="recolor-title">
        <h2 id="recolor-title">Tint and recolor</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Choose <strong>Tint / Selective Recolor</strong>.</li>
          <li>Use <strong>Whole image</strong> for an intentional full-image tint, or choose <strong>Mask image</strong> and provide a real grayscale/alpha mask.</li>
          <li>Choose <strong>Set absolute hue</strong> when the target hue should be stable regardless of the source hue. Choose <strong>Rotate existing hue</strong> for a relative shift.</li>
          <li>Adjust Saturation, Lightness, Chroma, Blend, and the conservative protection switches. Zero Blend or zero coverage leaves the source unchanged.</li>
          <li>Preview, inspect the result, then Apply. Apply creates a new embedded result layer; the source remains available.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          Lightness is source CIELAB L* preservation. It is not HSL lightness and does not promise
          calibrated linear-luminance preservation across arbitrary output profiles. Out-of-gamut
          target colors are clipped at the browser's sRGB RGBA8 boundary.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="palette-title">
        <h2 id="palette-title">Palette colorize</h2>
        <p>
          Select one or more document swatches. One color is valid for a tonal map. Shaded mapping
          keeps source lightness and can create tonal shades that are not literal swatch bytes.
          Strict mapping reaches only the selected sRGB colors at 100% adherence; at lower
          adherence it intentionally blends toward them and is no longer a strict constraint.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="reference-title">
        <h2 id="reference-title">Reference transfer and harmonize</h2>
        <p>
          Choose a separate image file. Varve passes both the reference identity and decoded pixels
          to the engine, validates empty/transparent references, ignores transparent border pixels
          in the statistics, and supports different source/reference dimensions. The result is a
          global color-distribution transfer; it does not know that a shirt in one image is the
          same object as a shirt in another.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="docs-section docs-section--note" aria-labelledby="photo-title">
        <h2 id="photo-title">Photo colorization readiness</h2>
        <p>
          Photo Colorization is disabled until Settings → Models reports a verified DDColor model.
          The current release includes the adapter, bounded preview, explicit letterbox geometry,
          tensor validation, and full-resolution reconstruction that combines predicted chroma
          with the original source detail and alpha. It does not ship an unverified checkpoint.
        </p>
        <p>
          If the model is unavailable, use Tint / Selective Recolor for deterministic work. Varve
          does not silently substitute a tint and label it photo AI, and it does not upload the
          source image as a fallback.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="review-title">
        <h2 id="review-title">Review, save, and export</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Preview is bounded for responsiveness; Apply Full may recompute a large image with more model context.</li>
          <li>A changed source or input revision makes an asynchronous result stale instead of replacing unrelated edits.</li>
          <li>Apply stores accepted result bytes in the document's embedded asset table, so save/reopen/export does not require the model again.</li>
          <li>The current result is materialized and source-preserving. Re-editable Colorize recipes and persistent painted hints are planned, not implied by the duplicate layer.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <aside class="docs-callout">
        <strong>Further reading</strong>
        <p><a href={sitePath('/features/colorization')}>Colorize &amp; Recolor feature overview</a> · <a href={sitePath('/docs/tools/color')}>Color &amp; Effects reference</a> · <a href="https://github.com/K-Arthur/varve/blob/main/docs/architecture/colorization-system.md">Engine contract and verification record</a></p>
      </aside>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .docs-page { max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0 5rem; }
  .breadcrumb { font-size: .875rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .docs-page h1 { max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 1rem; font: 700 clamp(2.3rem, 6vw, 4rem)/1.05 var(--font-editorial); color: var(--text-primary); letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  .docs-intro { max-width: 700px; margin-bottom: 3.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .docs-section { margin-bottom: 3.5rem; }
  .docs-section h2 { margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.65rem; }
  .docs-section h3 { margin-bottom: .5rem; color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .docs-section p, .docs-section li { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.75; }
  .docs-section p { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .docs-section ol, .docs-section ul { padding-left: 1.4rem; }
  .docs-section li { margin-bottom: .65rem; }
  .mode-table { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 1rem; }
  .mode-table article { padding: 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); background: var(--surface-card); }
  .mode-table article:first-child { border-color: var(--border-accent); background: var(--surface-accent-soft); }
  .mode-table p { margin-bottom: .8rem; }
  .mode-table span { color: var(--text-tertiary); font-size: .82rem; }
  .docs-section--note { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-primary); padding: 1.25rem 0 1.25rem 1.25rem; }
  .docs-callout { padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); background: var(--surface-muted); }
  .docs-callout strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .docs-callout p { margin: .5rem 0 0; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; }
  .docs-callout a { color: var(--text-link); }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .mode-table { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
